    "isNew": false,
    "codeLanguage": "javascript",
    "title": "Array.reduce()",
    "descriptionContent": "Aprende a reducir los valores de un array en un solo valor",
    "shortDescriptionContent": "",
    "showInTrack": true,
    "iconBanner": null,
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": 17477,
        "title": "Reducir",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 148361,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A veces, necesitamos convertir una serie de valores de un array en un solo valor. Por ejemplo, cuando queremos calcular una puntuación final.</p><p>Una forma clásica de hacer esto es a través de un bucle.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"77\" endIndex=\"82\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" points = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" score = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" element \" /><text value=\"of\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" points) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" score += element;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(score);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>score</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 148362,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Sin embargo, JavaScript ofrece un método más simple y ya existente. <code>.reduce()</code> puede combinar valores de un Array en un valor utilizando una función en línea.</p><p><code>.reduce()</code> utiliza la sintaxis: <code>ArrayName.reduce()</code>. Veamos cómo podríamos llamarlo en el array <code>points</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"list\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"43\" endIndex=\"49\" /><option startIndex=\"49\" endIndex=\"50\" /><option startIndex=\"50\" endIndex=\"56\" /><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"57\" /><option startIndex=\"57\" endIndex=\"58\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" points = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" score = points.reduce();\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>points</code> seguido de <code>.</code> y luego <code>reduce</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 148363,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para indicarle a la función <code>.reduce()</code> cómo combinar valores, primero necesitamos pasar una función como parámetro.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"57\" endIndex=\"65\" /><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"66\" /><option startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"67\" /><option startIndex=\"68\" endIndex=\"69\" /><option startIndex=\"69\" endIndex=\"70\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" points = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" score = points.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{});\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>function</code> seguido de <code>(</code> y luego <code>)</code>, <code>{</code>, <code>}</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 148364,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Nuestra función necesita dos parámetros: el primero para acceder al resultado de la <strong>reducción</strong> anterior, y el segundo para acceder al valor actual.</p><p>Agrega dos parámetros: <code>prev</code> y <code>curr</code>, en ese orden.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option startIndex=\"72\" endIndex=\"76\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" points = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" score = points.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prev, curr\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{});\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>prev,</code> seguido de <code>curr</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 148365,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><code>reduce()</code> itera a través de un array y, en cada valor, realiza una operación con los dos parámetros hasta que llega a un solo valor.</p><p>Por ejemplo, para totalizar una puntuación, la función en línea devuelve la suma de la reducción <code>prev</code> y el valor <code>curr</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"81\" endIndex=\"87\" /><option startIndex=\"88\" endIndex=\"99\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" points = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" score = points.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prev, curr\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prev + curr;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(score);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>return</code> seguido de <code>prev + curr</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 148366,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para simplificar nuestra sintaxis, podemos incorporar una función flecha de JavaScript en lugar de la función inline.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"57\" endIndex=\"75\" /><option startIndex=\"76\" endIndex=\"78\" /><option startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"96\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" points = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" score = points.reduce(\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prevVal, currVal\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") =&gt;\" /><text value=\" prevVal + currVal);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(score);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>(prevVal, currVal)</code> seguido de <code>=&gt;</code> y finalmente <code>prevVal + currVal</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 148367,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Si incluimos un tercer parámetro en la función, también podemos acceder al índice de cada iteración.</p><p>En este ejemplo, usamos <code>.reduce()</code> para sumar el <code>damage</code>, pero también incorporamos <code>index</code> para aplicar un multiplicador de combo de un segundo array.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"160\" endIndex=\"165\" /><option startIndex=\"214\" endIndex=\"219\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" damage = [\" /><text value=\"17.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20.25\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"24.75\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"13.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" comboMultiplier = [\" /><text value=\"0.9\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.9\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1.0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1.0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.9\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" totalDamage = damage.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prevVal, currVal, index\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prevVal + (currVal * comboMultiplier[index]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(totalDamage);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>index</code> seguido de <code>index</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 148368,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>¿Qué función de JavaScript podemos usar para convertir una serie de valores de un array en un solo valor?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>.reduce()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>.filter()</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>.reduce()</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 148369,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>¿Qué debemos pasar como parámetro para decirle a la función <code>.reduce()</code> cómo combinar valores?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Una función</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Una variable</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Una función.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 148370,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>¿A qué da acceso el primer parámetro de la función inline de <code>reduce()</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">El resultado de la reducción anterior</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">El valor del array de la iteración actual</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">El resultado de la reducción anterior.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 148371,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>¿A qué le da acceso el segundo parámetro de la función inline <code>reduce()</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">El valor del array de la iteración actual</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">El resultado de la reducción anterior</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">El valor del array de la iteración actual.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 148372,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>¿Qué podemos acceder al agregar un tercer parámetro opcional a la función?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">El índice</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">El array de llamada</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">El índice.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 148373,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Llama a la función <code>.reduce()</code> en el array <code>damage</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"68\" endIndex=\"74\" /><option startIndex=\"74\" endIndex=\"75\" /><option startIndex=\"75\" endIndex=\"81\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" damage = [\" /><text value=\"17.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20.25\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"24.75\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"13.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" totalDamage = damage.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prevVal, currVal\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prevVal + currVal;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(totalDamage);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>damage</code> seguido de <code>.</code> y finalmente <code>reduce</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #14",
            "id": 148374,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Agrega una función inline dentro de la función <code>.reduce()</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"59\" endIndex=\"67\" /><option startIndex=\"67\" endIndex=\"68\" /><option startIndex=\"68\" endIndex=\"69\" /><option startIndex=\"70\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option startIndex=\"71\" endIndex=\"72\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" drops = [\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" totalLoot = drops.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{});\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>function</code> seguido de <code>(</code> y luego <code>)</code>, <code>{</code>, <code>}</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #15",
            "id": 148375,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Agrega los parámetros apropiados para darle a la función inline acceso al valor de reducción anterior y al valor actual del array.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"68\" endIndex=\"72\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" drops = [\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" totalLoot = drops.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prev, curr\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prev * curr;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(totalLoot);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>prev</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #16",
            "id": 148376,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Queremos que la función <code>.reduce()</code> concatene todas las <code>parts</code> en un nombre de nivel.</p><p>Codifica la palabra clave correcta en la función inline para que devuelva el valor de reducción anterior concatenado con la parte actual.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"101\" endIndex=\"107\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" parts = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Level&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;1&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Boss&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Room&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" levelName = parts.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prev, curr\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prev + \" /><text value=\"&quot; &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + curr;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(levelName);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>return</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #17",
            "id": 148377,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Completa la función flecha de manera que <code>totalDamage</code> almacene la suma de los valores del array <code>damage</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"112\" endIndex=\"121\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" damage = [\" /><text value=\"17.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20.25\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"24.75\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"13.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" totalDamage = damage.reduce(\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prevVal, currVal\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") =&gt;\" /><text value=\" prevVal + currVal);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(totalDamage);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>+ currVal</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
